{
  "category": "Aqua Mouse Pokémon",
  "entries": [
    {
      "text": "The tip of its tail, which contains oil that is lighter than water, lets it swim without drowning.",
      "version": "gold"
    },
    {
      "text": "The end of its tail serves as a buoy that keeps it from drowning, even in a vicious current.",
      "version": "silver"
    },
    {
      "text": "The fur on its body naturally repels water. It can stay dry, even when it plays in the water.",
      "version": "crystal"
    },
    {
      "text": "MARILL’s oil-filled tail acts much like a life preserver. If you see just its tail bobbing on the water’s surface, it’s a sure indication that this POKéMON is diving beneath the water to feed on aquatic plants.",
      "version": "ruby"
    },
    {
      "text": "When fishing for food at the edge of a fast-running stream, MARILL wraps its tail around the trunk of a tree. This POKéMON’s tail is flexible and configured to stretch.",
      "version": "sapphire"
    },
    {
      "text": "Its body is covered with water-repellent fur. Because of the fur, it can swim through water at high speed without being slowed by the water’s resistance.",
      "version": "emerald"
    },
    {
      "text": "The end of its tail serves as a buoy that keeps it from drowning, even in a vicious current.",
      "version": "firered"
    },
    {
      "text": "The tip of its tail, which contains oil that is lighter than water, lets it swim without drowning.",
      "version": "leafgreen"
    },
    {
      "text": "Using its tail as a float, it dives underwater. It likes eating plants that grow on river bottoms.",
      "version": "diamond"
    },
    {
      "text": "The tip of its tail is filled with oil that is lighter than water, so it acts as a float.",
      "version": "pearl"
    },
    {
      "text": "The oil-filled end of its tail floats on water. It keeps MARILL from drowning even in a strong current.",
      "version": "platinum"
    },
    {
      "text": "The tip of its tail, which contains oil that is lighter than water, lets it swim without drowning.",
      "version": "heartgold"
